  "articleBody": "When your roof needs attention, it's easy to get caught up in common myths that might lead you down the wrong path. Let's clear up some misunderstandings about roof repair versus replacement so you can make a truly informed decision.\n\n- **Myth: Repairs are always the cheaper option, no matter what.**\n  **Fact:** While repairs have a lower initial price, this isn't always the most cost-effective solution in the long run. If your roof has widespread damage, is old, or has recurring issues, multiple repairs can add up quickly, often exceeding the cost of a full replacement over time. Plus, a new roof gives you a fresh start with new warranties and improved protection, especially against Texas's tough weather.\n\n- **Myth: You can just keep adding new shingle layers indefinitely.**\n  **Fact:** Not true! Many jurisdictions have regulations about how many layers of roofing can be on a structure. Covering too many existing layers is a frequent mistake. Plus, adding layers without removing old ones can add excessive weight, mask underlying deck issues, and reduce the effectiveness of new materials. Local building codes often require existing layers to be removed under certain conditions.\n\n- **Myth: A quick visual check from the ground is enough to decide.**\n  **Fact:** While a ground-level check can spot obvious issues, it's not a substitute for a professional, roof-level inspection. Many problems, like subtle hail damage, flashing issues, or soft spots on the decking, aren't visible from below. A comprehensive assessment includes documenting damage with photos and checking interior evidence like attic leaks, something Discounted Roofing Co. does during its free inspections.\n\n- **Myth: All roofers will give you the same repair or replacement recommendation.**\n  **Fact:** Recommendations can vary. Some contractors might push for a replacement when a repair is feasible, or vice versa. It’s crucial to get detailed, written scopes of work from different reputable companies and compare what they're offering, not just the headline price. Discounted Roofing Co. offers honest recommendations, explaining clearly if a replacement is truly needed or if repairs are enough, and helping you understand if damage is likely to qualify for a claim.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}